Q: How to use uncopyable components with skypjack/entt? A: <p>Moments after asking, I got a working solution;</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>// check the count (maybe? it worked correctly with the immobile components)
REQUIRE(1 == reg.view&lt;component&gt;().size_hint());

// examine them in loops like this
// ... idk why, but, the other styles of loops didn't work with immobile components
auto view = reg.view&lt;component&gt;();
for (auto [e, com] : view.each())
{
    ???
}
</code></pre>
<p>The later for-loop works. Other (read only) loops I tried didn't when the components were immobile.</p>

Q: Printing JSON strings in a loop renders invalid output A: <ul>
<li>The controller should not be interacting with the database.</li>
<li>The model should receive all relevant parameters regardless of the call site or source of the input values.</li>
<li>The loop seems pointless because a maximum of one user should be able to sign in with a given set of credentials. I can't imagine the loop is the problem.</li>
<li>The <code>||</code> operator in the elseif will parse without an error and <code>&quot;Pending&quot;</code> <a href="https://3v4l.org/0SvmW#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">will evaluate as <code>true</code></a> therefore killing your loop, but again if the lone row didn't Pass, then &quot;no login&quot; is the desired behavior. I would use <code>in_array()</code> if retaining that logic.</li>
<li>We don't know if your credential checking method or database data is at fault.</li>
<li>It will be impossible for a row to contain a Pending row while also not having any rows in the result set - so that part is ...weird.</li>
<li>More generally, this style of login authentication is outdated and passwords shouldn't be checked via a query. More modern approaches fetch the password hash and verify it with a non-SQL server-side language.</li>
</ul>
<p>I'll advise a rewrite, but it still might not resolve your problem if there is an issue with the data or hashing process.</p>
<p>controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function logsig()
{
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('Login_model', 'LoginModel');
    $username = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('username');
    $status = $this-&gt;LoginModel-&gt;attemptLogin(
        $username,
        $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('password')
    );
    $sessionState = false;
    if ($status === 'Pass') {
        $this-&gt;session-&gt;set_userdata(['logged' =&gt; &quot;1&quot;, 'username' =&gt; &quot;$username&quot;]);
        $sessionState = true;
    }
    // You might want to alert the user if the status is Pending
    header('Content-type:application/json');
    echo json_encode(['session_state' =&gt; $sessionState]);
}
</code></pre>
<p>model:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function attemptLogin(string $username, string $password): ?string
{
    $row = $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;get_where('users', ['username' =&gt; $username, 'status' =&gt; 'Pass'])
        -&gt;row();

    if (!$row || !password_verify($password, $row-&gt;password)) {
        return null;
    }
    return $row-&gt;status;
}
</code></pre>
